00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:01,472
You need an operation.
You have appendicitis.

244
00:12:01,555 --> 00:12:04,141
Oh! Who called it?
Nothing but net.

245
00:12:04,225 --> 00:12:05,476
How long will he be gone?

246
00:12:05,601 --> 00:12:06,852
Two or three days.

247
00:12:07,436 --> 00:12:09,063
Don't remember me like this.

248
00:12:09,146 --> 00:12:11,732
Remember me as the man
who pulled down the screen.

249
00:12:11,816 --> 00:12:12,900
Drama queen, am I right?

250
00:12:16,237 --> 00:12:18,656
Philip, if you're
hearing this memo,

251
00:12:18,823 --> 00:12:21,242
that can only mean
one thing, I am dead.

252
00:12:21,534 --> 00:12:26,247
You are the rightful heir to Schrute Farms.
Please, you must do one thing.

253
00:12:26,330 --> 00:12:28,833
Kill Mose before he kills you.

254
00:12:32,711 --> 00:12:34,839
Mose. Hey, it's Dwight.

255
00:12:34,922 --> 00:12:36,507
Listen, yeah, I just want
to give you a heads up.

256
00:12:36,590 --> 00:12:37,967
That was
an interesting diversion.

257
00:12:38,092 --> 00:12:39,510
Should we get
back to the meeting?

258
00:12:40,594 --> 00:12:42,388
Woah. Are those mini pizzas?

259
00:12:42,513 --> 00:12:44,640
Yeah. I figure if
we keep things savory

260
00:12:44,765 --> 00:12:46,892
while Oscar's mouth
is in canker country...

261
00:12:46,976 --> 00:12:49,228
I also have some
bacon-wrapped dates on deck.

262
00:12:49,311 --> 00:12:53,399
Look at these little mini pizzas.
Does this make me look huge?

263
00:12:54,525 --> 00:12:57,611
Hey, guys,
look at me, I'm huge.

264
00:12:58,404 --> 00:13:00,990
Hey, Darryl, good news,
your fax went through.

265
00:13:01,198 --> 00:13:03,534
On  yeah.

266
00:13:03,617 --> 00:13:04,702
UP high.

267
00:13:04,869 --> 00:13:05,953
Yes, sir. Thanks.

268
00:13:06,203 --> 00:13:09,498
Dunder Mifflin, this is Andy. I put
out some new magazines. Check it out.

269
00:13:09,623 --> 00:13:11,083
Ah, Dwell.

270
00:13:15,004 --> 00:13:17,882
I'm acting like I like
Reception, and I'm a really good actor

271
00:13:17,965 --> 00:13:21,427
so people are actually buying
that I actually like Reception.

272
00:13:21,510 --> 00:13:24,388
But I mean,
seriously, Reception sucks.

273
00:13:24,722 --> 00:13:26,056
Ooh! There's the phone!

274
00:13:27,099 --> 00:13:28,559
I just
got out of surgery.

275
00:13:29,351 --> 00:13:30,936
What's going on? Fill me in.

276
00:13:31,228 --> 00:13:34,231
Well, we broke into groups and the
groups are giving presentations later.

277
00:13:34,565 --> 00:13:36,066
Who's doing the presentations?

278
00:13:36,567 --> 00:13:37,735
Packer's giving one.

279
00:13:37,985 --> 00:13:39,570
Jim will probably
give ours, I guess.

280
00:13:39,695 --> 00:13:40,696
Damn it!

281
00:13:41,322 --> 00:13:43,657
Let's see.
What else have you missed?

282
00:13:43,866 --> 00:13:46,035
Ryan switched his
nametag to his pants,

283
00:13:46,118 --> 00:13:47,578
so now it's like
if you wear yours

284
00:13:47,703 --> 00:13:49,121
on your shirt,
you're a total dip.

285
00:13:49,205 --> 00:13:51,290
But if you switch,
you're a copycat.

286
00:13:51,415 --> 00:13:53,542
But I think I
figured out a solution.

287
00:13:54,710 --> 00:13:57,421
What else? My shoes are...

288
00:13:58,005 --> 00:14:00,257
...features the tech support area.
Bring in your product,

289
00:14:00,341 --> 00:14:02,843
a bunch of nerdy
virgins fix it on the spot.

290
00:14:02,927 --> 00:14:04,261
Huge for building loyalty.

291
00:14:04,345 --> 00:14:06,096
Yes, that is
a very good point.

292
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:07,806
Yeah, Todd, decent idea.

293
00:14:08,557 --> 00:14:10,893
Obvious, but interesting.

294
00:14:11,018 --> 00:14:12,561
Dwight, are you all right?

295
00:14:12,686 --> 00:14:14,146
I'm great. How are you?

296
00:14:18,776 --> 00:14:19,777
Uh...

297
00:14:21,946 --> 00:14:23,447
What's our presentation about?

298
00:14:23,531 --> 00:14:24,657
Dwight, will you go
back to the hospital?

299
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:26,158
You were there for
like three hours.

300
00:14:26,242 --> 00:14:27,785
I got the surgery.
What else is there to do?

301
00:14:28,035 --> 00:14:29,787
Do 100 jumping jacks.
No. I don't feel like it.

302
00:14:29,870 --> 00:14:31,080
You do 100 jumping jacks.

303
00:14:31,163 --> 00:14:32,331
I don't feel like it either.

304
00:14:32,581 --> 00:14:34,959
...ninety-seven, 98, 99...

305
00:14:35,417 --> 00:14:36,710
I want the Vice Presidency.

306
00:14:36,794 --> 00:14:38,087
You haven't done
any of the research.

307
00:14:38,170 --> 00:14:40,881
You're too slow. You're too small.
Seabiscuit is a stupid name.

308
00:14:40,965 --> 00:14:42,633
You guys sound just like
the enemies of Seabiscuit.

309
00:14:42,925 --> 00:14:44,176
I'm going to do it.

310
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:45,761
Oh, let him do it.

311
00:14:46,887 --> 00:14:47,972
Stanley,
are you listening to music?

312
00:14:48,138 --> 00:14:49,223
Yep.

313
00:14:50,307 --> 00:14:53,060
All right, who's ready
for the next presentation?

314
00:14:53,394 --> 00:14:55,312
Oh... What is your topic?

315
00:14:56,355 --> 00:14:59,233
What is our topic? Oh, what
a topic it is. Mmm-hmm.

316
00:14:59,441 --> 00:15:00,818
Retail consumer habits.

317
00:15:01,277 --> 00:15:02,861
Really? Okay.

318
00:15:03,153 --> 00:15:05,614
Retail consumer habits is...

319
00:15:08,325 --> 00:15:09,368
The only thing
you need to know

320
00:15:09,451 --> 00:15:10,744
about retail
consumer habits is that

321
00:15:10,828 --> 00:15:13,247
consumers are
mindless lemmings.

322
00:15:13,330 --> 00:15:15,833
They just want to
be told what to do.

323
00:15:17,751 --> 00:15:22,381
Fast-forward to today, and the
retail consumer is independent,

324
00:15:22,673 --> 00:15:26,802
well-informed, super smart.
Super smart.

325
00:15:27,511 --> 00:15:28,512
Okay.

326
00:15:30,931 --> 00:15:34,602
Shopping habits are both
seasonal and cyclical.

327
00:15:34,685 --> 00:15:35,811
What does this mean?

328
00:15:35,894 --> 00:15:36,979
I can field this one.

329
00:15:37,104 --> 00:15:38,188
No, sit down.

330
00:15:38,272 --> 00:15:42,985
Seasonal, well, the Christmas shopping
season is certainly a busy one.

331
00:15:43,068 --> 00:15:44,778
Back to school is as well,

332
00:15:44,862 --> 00:15:47,114
and in early summer
it seems to slow down a bit.

333
00:15:47,197 --> 00:15:48,949
But shopping is also cyclical.

334
00:15:49,033 --> 00:15:53,287
The menstrual cycle determines
every choice a woman makes.

335
00:15:53,704 --> 00:15:58,709
You see, during ovulation, a woman's
only goal is to get pregnant.

336
00:15:58,917 --> 00:16:02,379
During menses, she is sad
that she has failed.

337
00:16:02,504 --> 00:16:05,299
And how does
the woman console herself?

338
00:16:05,382 --> 00:16:07,760
Shopping. Shopping.

339
00:16:07,843 --> 00:16:10,721
Just, Jim, could you fetch me
some ice chips?

340
00:16:13,390 --> 00:16:17,978
Thank you. Just gonna take a
brief pause at this point.

341
00:16:18,562 --> 00:16:19,563
Thank you.

342
00:16:21,065 --> 00:16:22,483
Oh, God.

343
00:16:25,527 --> 00:16:26,737
Next slide.

344
00:16:29,198 --> 00:16:30,824
Mail call!

345
00:16:30,908 --> 00:16:33,952
His name is Oscar,
and he's got some mail

346
00:16:34,036 --> 00:16:37,998
And he better open it or go to
jail, 'cause it's your taxes

347
00:16:38,082 --> 00:16:41,168
His name is Kevin,
and no mail for him

348
00:16:41,251 --> 00:16:44,505
But he got a coupon
for some frozen yogurt

349
00:16:45,923 --> 00:16:47,508
Are those the lyrics?

350
00:16:47,591 --> 00:16:49,426
"Anderson's Three Pillars
of Retail."

351
00:16:49,510 --> 00:16:51,762
Crucial. So important.

352
00:16:54,098 --> 00:16:55,224
Next.

353
00:16:56,350 --> 00:16:57,810
Are there any questions?

354
00:16:58,435 --> 00:17:01,480
What are the Three
Pillars of Retail?

355
00:17:03,732 --> 00:17:05,776
Convenience.
Ingredients.

356
00:17:06,235 --> 00:17:07,861
Service.
Burgers.

357
00:17:08,028 --> 00:17:09,029
Building loyalty.

358
00:17:09,154 --> 00:17:10,197
Killing royalty.

359
00:17:11,073 --> 00:17:12,491
But truth be told,
we should really

360
00:17:12,574 --> 00:17:14,284
disregard
Anderson's Three Pillars.

361
00:17:14,993 --> 00:17:17,246
He was later
diagnosed with dementia.

362
00:17:17,746 --> 00:17:20,124
You know what is important?

363
00:17:20,207 --> 00:17:24,628
Is Dwight's pillars,
and there's only one, desire.

364
00:17:25,170 --> 00:17:28,590
Do we have a desire
to dominate the retail space?

365
00:17:28,674 --> 00:17:30,718
Not just succeed in it
but to dominate.

366
00:17:30,801 --> 00:17:33,137
And looking around this room,
I'm not so sure that we do.

367
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:34,221
But we can get there.

368
00:17:34,304 --> 00:17:38,434
And I can lead us there,
and that is all that matters.

369
00:17:38,642 --> 00:17:41,145
Very true. Where there's
a will, there's a way.

370
00:17:41,228 --> 00:17:43,939
I once spent
a passionate night

371
00:17:44,064 --> 00:17:46,734
with Hugh Grant's brother,
John Grant.

372
00:17:46,817 --> 00:17:50,154
He's older than Hugh,
just a little bit uglier.

373
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:51,530
How did I pull that off?

374
00:17:51,989 --> 00:17:54,116
Sheer force of will.

375
00:17:54,199 --> 00:17:55,492
That is very good, Dwight.

376
00:17:55,743 --> 00:17:57,870
Thank you very much.
Any other questions?

377
00:17:58,412 --> 00:17:59,913
Jim.

378
00:18:00,038 --> 00:18:01,540
You are bleeding
through your shirt.

379
00:18:02,958 --> 00:18:03,959
Oops.

380
00:18:05,544 --> 00:18:08,839
That's embarrassing.
Egg on my face.

381
00:18:10,674 --> 00:18:11,675
Ah...

382
00:18:13,469 --> 00:18:15,471
Hey, having fun?

383
00:18:15,596 --> 00:18:17,598
Yes, I am,
as a matter of fact.

384
00:18:17,681 --> 00:18:20,517
Oh, I know how it is.
I know it's a lot of fun.

385
00:18:20,601 --> 00:18:22,686
I don't know how it is.
Andy, this is a lame job.

386
00:18:22,770 --> 00:18:24,146
What are you doing here?

387
00:18:25,147 --> 00:18:26,356
I found my calling.

388
00:18:26,648 --> 00:18:31,862
Andy, when I was 12 years old, we did
a field trip, a lock-in at the zoo.

389
00:18:32,654 --> 00:18:37,576
I met this girl. I thought she was so perfect.
I was in love with her.

390
00:18:38,202 --> 00:18:41,038
But when the sun came up,
I knew it wasn't real

391
00:18:41,121 --> 00:18:44,249
because she was ugly
and I had grown tired of her.

392
00:18:45,209 --> 00:18:46,710
I know you want
Reception today,

393
00:18:46,877 --> 00:18:48,420
but tomorrow you
won't want to do her.

394
00:18:48,504 --> 00:18:50,005
She's a dog.

395
00:18:50,923 --> 00:18:52,841
Guys, I don't
like this analogy.

396
00:18:54,218 --> 00:18:56,512
Oh, fine.

397
00:19:02,643 --> 00:19:03,685
Did you see this?

398
00:19:03,769 --> 00:19:04,770
It's nice.

399
00:19:04,895 --> 00:19:05,938
I mean...

400
00:19:09,233 --> 00:19:10,442
How are you feeling?

401
00:19:10,567 --> 00:19:11,819
Amazing.

402
00:19:11,902 --> 00:19:13,403
Just lost four
ounces of appendix,

403
00:19:13,529 --> 00:19:15,072
already replaced
it with muscle.

404
00:19:15,531 --> 00:19:17,282
Can I see the wound?

405
00:19:22,746 --> 00:19:25,958
Oh, that's disgusting.
That's barely healed.

406
00:19:26,041 --> 00:19:29,002
You're not paying me to heal.
You're paying me to kick ass.

407
00:19:29,253 --> 00:19:33,757
A few hours ago, your body
was open like a cabinet.

408
00:19:34,633 --> 00:19:36,134
That's right.
That is amazing.

409
00:19:36,218 --> 00:19:37,469
Todd, look at that.

410
00:19:37,594 --> 00:19:38,846
Ch, yikes!

411
00:19:38,929 --> 00:19:40,055
Incoming.

412
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:41,265
Not so fast.

413
00:19:41,348 --> 00:19:42,933
Would you come
in early tomorrow,

414
00:19:43,016 --> 00:19:45,102
so we could talk about the
store over breakfast?

415
00:19:45,519 --> 00:19:48,230
I feel you have
a lot to offer.

416
00:19:48,355 --> 00:19:49,606
It would be an honor, ma'am.

417
00:19:49,690 --> 00:19:52,651
I'll go ahead and cancel
my post-op checkup right now.

418
00:19:53,151 --> 00:19:54,444
I had two goals today,

419
00:19:54,528 --> 00:19:57,906
the first was to make myself the
clear candidate for Vice President.

420
00:19:57,990 --> 00:20:00,659
I achieved that,
no thanks to my appendix.

421
00:20:00,742 --> 00:20:03,620
The second was to find a
memorable souvenir for Philip.

422
00:20:03,704 --> 00:20:06,957
For that, I do have
to thank my appendix.

423
00:20:18,135 --> 00:20:19,887
Dunder Mifflin, how can I
help you save money on paper?

424
00:20:19,970 --> 00:20:21,638
This is Andrew.

425
00:20:21,763 --> 00:20:23,390
Hi, Andrew.
What happened to Erin?

426
00:20:23,473 --> 00:20:26,184
Oh, she's on an assignment in
Florida for a couple weeks.

427
00:20:26,268 --> 00:20:28,395
Oh, good for her.
She's such a sweetheart.

428
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:30,689
You tell her Donna
Moraski misses her.

429
00:20:30,772 --> 00:20:33,066
I miss her, too.

430
00:20:35,611 --> 00:20:37,738
Everyone, we have
a very special guest.

431
00:20:37,821 --> 00:20:42,242
He turned an idea into a store,
into hundreds of stores.

432
00:20:42,326 --> 00:20:46,413
I give you Wally Amos, founder
of Famous Amos cookies.

433
00:20:46,496 --> 00:20:47,581
Yeah!

434
00:20:51,543 --> 00:20:53,337
So I hear
you're all looking to

435
00:20:53,503 --> 00:20:55,339
bake up some dough
in the sales game.

436
00:20:55,631 --> 00:20:58,425
Well, back when I
was regular Amos...

437
00:20:58,508 --> 00:20:59,635
What's under the cloth?

438
00:20:59,718 --> 00:21:01,178
We'll get to that.

439
00:21:01,303 --> 00:21:02,763
Cookies. I bet you
anything it's cookies.

440
00:21:03,180 --> 00:21:04,514
It's cookies.

441
00:21:04,598 --> 00:21:06,975
Let me finish my speech first.

442
00:21:07,184 --> 00:21:10,646
Oh, we get the gist. It's just
success and effort, isn't it?

443
00:21:10,729 --> 00:21:13,565
So just don't be coy.
Make with the cookies.

444
00:21:13,649 --> 00:21:16,526
Cookies.

445
00:21:18,195 --> 00:21:19,446
Famous, hi.

446
00:21:19,529 --> 00:21:22,157
I'm sure you get ideas
for new cookies all the time.

447
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:25,452
But I...
Is it oatmeal with no raisins?

448
00:21:25,535 --> 00:21:26,662
I'm sorry to have
wasted your time.

449
00:21:26,787 --> 00:21:27,871
That's okay.
Thank you very much.

